  "summary": "MRCL2Suhail exfiltrates current-directory listing to pinggy tunnel on import",
  "details": "On `import MRCL2Suhail`, the package's `__init__.py` imports `.core`, whose module-level code enumerates the current working directory with `os.listdir('.')` and opens a TCP connection via `socket.create_connection` to the hardcoded host `vxtuv-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link:34367`, sending the file listing over the socket. The destination is an anonymous pinggy-free.link reverse-tunnel fronting IP 13.205.45.209, not a documented first-party endpoint, and the README advertises the package as a document-integrity demonstration with no mention of outbound network activity. Any Python process that imports this package discloses the contents of its working directory to that remote host at import time, with no opt-in, no configuration, and no gating.",
